# @jxnvigoel19/agent-loop-guard

A zero-dependency circuit breaker for AI agents in Node.js. Stops tool-calling agents from burning API credits in infinite repetition loops (`A -> A -> A`) or oscillating ping-pong loops (`A -> B -> A -> B`).

## Installation

```bash
npm install @jxnvigoel19/agent-loop-guard
```

## Usage

```javascript
const { createLoopGuard } = require("@jxnvigoel19/agent-loop-guard");

const guard = createLoopGuard({
  maxIdenticalCalls: 2,
  windowSize: 10
});

const tools = guard.wrapAll({
  searchWeb: async ({ query }) => {
    return `Results for ${query}`;
  }
});

// Call inside your agent loop
async function run() {
  const output = await tools.searchWeb({ query: "latest AI news" });
  console.log(output);
}

run();
```

## API

- `createLoopGuard(options)` — Creates a new guard instance.
- `guard.wrap(toolName, fn)` — Wraps a single tool function.
- `guard.wrapAll(toolsObj)` — Wraps every function inside a tools object.
- `guard.reset()` — Clears history between separate agent runs.
